"""Long mixed conversations (r2, written blind 2026-10-22 from docs/14, docs/17, knowledge/ only): 10-25 turns that
mix questions about Lumi and Cutshion (facts exactly as in knowledge/; what is not there must be said as not known,
never a number), the weather and the time, commands (move, turn, look with corrections and "a bit more", wave after
an ability question and "show me", go to a marker of the dialogue's map with "where are you going?" and stop, a place
not on the map with "why?", follow with a question on the way and a stop word, songs listed / sung / stopped, chains,
the hand when holding), seeing turns whose scene changes (fresh look, a wrong correction checked against the camera),
follow-ups about Lumi's last answer (why / how / really / 왜 / 진짜), the visitor correcting their own question,
conditions / remarks / words to someone else (nothing moves), back-channels, topic changes and sometimes a goodbye.
English, Korean (반말 / 해요체 / 하십시오체) and mixed / Konglish, whisper slips ("wether", "hau tall", "follow mi", "wai").

DIALOGUES = [{"who", "topic", "lang": "en" | "ko" | "mix", "map", "markers", "state": "idle" | "holding" (at the
start), "turns": [turn, ...]}]
turn = {"say", "reply" (only on setup turns), "scored", "expect_action", "must", "must_not", "check"} plus optional
"scene" and "route".
- scored False with "reply": a setup, put the reply into the history as Lumi's, do not generate or score it. scored
  False without "reply": a back-channel or greeting, answered, not judged.
- expect_action: "none" (talk) or the round 1 command notation, alternatives split by " | ": action:<a> [words]
  ("action:look me | action:look center", "action:move back 0.3", "action:go_to stage | mission", "action:wave |
  refuse", "action:follow | refuse"), "stop", "status" (answered from the task state / trip), "sing", "give",
  "place | action:put down", "refuse", "end" (goodbye), "chain" (several parts in the order said). "status | none" /
  "refuse | none": either is right. A motion not listed is wrong.
- must / must_not: case-insensitive regexes on the spoken reply (every must matches, no must_not does); empty on
  most command turns (the action is what is judged).
- scene (seeing turns only): the seeing_dialogues format (people with id, dist_m, side, top, bottom, left_hand,
  right_hand (the person's own hands), hands_visible, raised; objects); "A" is the speaker. Answers come from the
  scene of that turn, never from what was said before.
- route: talk | seeing | act | status | end (what kind of turn it is, for the report).
- map / markers: the fake map of tests/blind/maps.py the place commands are on (hand it to the reader).

held-out: only scored, never read by whoever fixes the code.
"""

